Sikarugir's Wine 11 wineserver has one extra request, flush_key_done, right after
flush_key (from the registry-flush patches it carries). Requests are numbered by
position, so without it every request the driver sends after that point reaches the
wrong handler: set_queue_fd never happens, the thread is never told about Mac events,
and games get no mouse or keyboard input. Nokcandu also checks an engine's request
table before installing the driver (WindowedPresentation.serverRequestsMatch).

--- a/include/wine/server_protocol.h
+++ b/include/wine/server_protocol.h
@@ -6253,2 +6253,3 @@
     REQ_flush_key,
+    REQ_flush_key_done,
     REQ_enum_key,
